.IX Title "List::SomeUtils::XS 3pm"
.TH List::SomeUtils::XS 3pm 2026-06-22 "perl v5.40.1" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
List::SomeUtils::XS \- XS implementation for List::SomeUtils
.SH VERSION
.IX Header "VERSION"
version 0.59
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
There are no user-facing parts here. See List::SomeUtils for API details.
.PP
You shouldn't have to install this module directly. When you install
List::SomeUtils, it checks whether your system has a compiler. If it does,
then it adds a dependency on this module so that it gets installed and you have
the faster XS implementation.
.PP
This distribution requires List::SomeUtils but to avoid a circular
dependency, that dependency is explicitly left out from the this distribution's
metadata. However, without LSU already installed this module cannot function.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.IX Header "SEE ALSO"
List::Util, List::AllUtils
